    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0461" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.35112 RP/2–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-24T14:00:00-03:00">February 24,
                            1945—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 24—12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>373. Fiore has submitted to Embassy list of 44 German firms intervened to date.
                    This figure comprises 19 principal companies and 25 subsidiaries. List being
                    forwarded by pouch.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d315-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>He also advises that Perón<anchor n="94" xml:id="d315-f2"/> is exercising
                    pressure on him to go easy on the intervention of certain German firms because
                    of existing <pb facs="0462" n="448" xml:id="pg448"/> army contracts with them;
                    Fiore claims he will not yield to this pressure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d315-f1" n="93" xml:id="d315-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch 17,373, February 24, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d315-f2" n="94" xml:id="d315-f2-content">
                <p>Juan D. Perón, Vice President and Minister of War.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
